<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Aga sees 50,000 T sugar exports.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Aga sees 50,000 T sugar exports.</headline>
<dateline>GUADALAJARA, Mexico 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Consorcio Aga SA will export about 50,000 tonnes of refined white sugar this year, the company's director general, Abelardo Garciarce, said Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We will be exporting around 50,000 tonnes of sugar this year...to the United States and to world spot markets,&quot; Garciarce told reporters.</p>
<p>In April, Aga started exporting for the first time with about 20,000 tonnes of refined whites sent to Somalia in Africa. Aga has two sugar mills, one in the state of Nayarit and another in Sinaloa, producing around 200,000 per harvest.</p>
<p>((--Monica Ballesca, Guadalajara bureau +523 817-0397))</p>
